WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:08.870 align:start position:0%
 
oh  well the strain has just wrapped up his  first season and since i did a review of  the premiere episode i thought it was  only fitting for me to come back  and talk about the first season overall  now to consider this your spoiler  warning because i am going to be  talking about the entire show up to and  including the recently aired season  finale  the short spoiler-free version is that  this show became an exercise in  frustration for me  now i do make an attempt to try and  divorce  my expectations of what i wish something  was and accept it for what it actually  is now i don't always succeed in that  i'll be the first to admit that  and i really was unable to remove  what i'd hoped this show would be from  the final result but i actually blamed  the show for that because it repeatedly  dangled interesting and unique aspects  and plot points  to either immediately ignore them or  yank them away  here's an early example of what i'm  talking about the first few episodes did  a lot of really good  build up and had a lot of tension around  the four survivors  of the plane disaster that was shown in  the pilot one of them in particular  really intrigued me with how his handle  i dealt with this husband  and father and he came home and he was  starting to undergo the physical changes  that you would associate with someone  becoming a vampire  now his wife could tell something was  wrong and she could  just sort of sense that it was dangerous  she arranged for her kids  to be sent off somewhere safe but she  stayed behind she stayed behind to try  and help him  even as he became clearly visibly less  human and just more unhinged with his  own last bit of humanity he locked  himself  in their shed and she even after he's  locked away and he's not even a  semblance of humanity left  she arranges for a neighbor to open that  shed so her husband can feed  this is a phenomenal intriguing  deep heavy setup i mean honestly it's  the sort of thing that could almost  support its own series how far will this  woman go  for the man that she loves even though  he is clearly not that person anymore  well immediately at the start of the  next episode turns out  she killed herself and then the heroes  of the show off the husband and that's  it they move on  and it's just such a waste of an amazing  and intriguing setup i mean i understand  that wasn't the main point of the show  they weren't going to string it along  forever but  they set it up and then literally did  nothing  it keeps hitting these forks on the  roads where it could do something  interesting and dynamic and unusual and  always opts for the obvious cliched  option if you watch my review of the  pilot you may remember what i talked  about ephraim goodweather and how i  really liked him when he was focusing on  this disease and he was working on that  and i was concerned about  the family dramatics with his ex-wife  and his son  taking over his character well take a  wild guess what happened  the guy just gets so bogged down in this  tired very obvious  line of family drama that pretty much  the scientific aspect of his character  gets pretty much  dropped around the fifth episode  altogether and all he does is  argue with the old man who clearly knows  what is going on they in fact  the guy points out to ephraim repeatedly  hasn't everything i said been true yes  it has only an idiot would keep  questioning him what does this guy keep  doing  and speaking of the old man it brings up  another point this show has got the  wrong  main characters the most interesting and  dynamic and  fun characters by far are vasily fett  who's an exterminator he's just a fun  character he's the guy that is the most  enjoyable to watch in these sorts of  scenarios which is that he's not in  denial  he's not gonna go oh my god how could  this be happening he's gonna observe  what's going on and just  roll with it he's gonna do whatever he  has to do to survive he's not going to  question the scenario he's going to just  fight against it right off the bat  and the other really good one is the  character of abraham sutrakian now  admittedly it's a slightly cliched  character in a vampire setup  it's abraham van helsing basically but  he's so well played by david bradley and  given some really phenomenal backstory  from his history as a concentration camp  survivor  that it works it works really well and  actually  this should have been a wake-up call to  the makers of this show because when  your flashback is more interesting than  what's going on  in the main story it's a sign that maybe  you need to work this  a little bit better but they're clearly  not the main characters they're always  side characters our heroes are supposed  to be  ephraim and nora and nora is even  worse than ephram is she exhausts so  much physical and emotional energy  trying to save and then shelter her  mother with alzheimer's hmm i wonder how  this little bit's gonna turn out  exactly how you think it is and hope for  no particular reason nora and ephraim  are  occasionally lovers why because that's  just what happens with your male and  female leads that's what they do  no you don't need to be doing that it  serves no function  serves no point in fact they get caught  by another character who says oh  in the middle of a play do you find time  to get busy on the rug that is exactly  what i was asking  in the way the entire infection unfolds  i never felt like i had a really good  picture  of how this thing was spreading because  how  big or small or where the infection was  located within the city of new york  completely varied from episode to  episode pretty much just depending on  what that episode needed it to be  so you've got some episodes where it  seems like the entire city is just  overrun with vampires you can't get away  with them there's other times they're  almost nowhere to be seen  the place is just like a ghost town and  you get no effective sort of birds out  here like oh there's the heart of the  infection it's spreading out from there  well no it's there  and it's there and it's oh wait but it's  not there anymore because now the  heroes are there and there's no  another example of just doing the most  contrived convenient style of writing  is the limited communications it's a  fairly important plot point that  a group of hackers gets hired to just  bring down the internet in new york city  now setting aside how  plausible that even is in the first  place the show is completely  inconsistent on how effective it is  because there are times when  if the story needs it they can't even  get a text message to each other there  are other times that are actually able  to surf the internet as  normal albeit somewhat slowly just long  enough  to get a vital piece of information then  the internet goes down again  this is the absolute epitome of  contrived convenient  storytelling it doesn't even follow any  kind of internal logic  now again if you saw my review of the  pilot you may have mentioned that i said  guillermo del toro who's one of the  creators and directed that pilot seemed  to be ripping himself off a little bit  specifically borrowing from blade 2.  well change ripping off a little bit to  ripping off  wholesale really this story is blade 2  without blade  the newly effective vampires are handled  pretty much identical  to the reapers in blade 2 down to the  loss of  all body hair the protruding stinger  that is used to both  feed and infect others having vampires  function really more like zombies than  proper vampires heck i'm pretty sure i  even saw  some of those vampires doing the  sideways reaper scuttle  and it's not even just with the vampires  they're ripping off blade too remember  the uv light bombs  they're back sewers infested with  massive nests of vampires yup  check that off the list too now even if  you've never seen blade 2 and wouldn't  recognize  all that stuff that it's ripping off the  show is incredibly repetitive just unto  itself  i lost count of how many times the show  re-emphasizes  the newly infected go after their loved  ones it was made  pretty clear and by about the fourth  episode this was made very clear in the  first few times it was very effective  but it just keeps  hitting that same note again and again  and again  not to mention just the progress of the  infection gets played out repeatedly  again  even though we've seen the entire cycle  by the third or fourth episode  there's another character a gus he has  like a little bit that's actually  relevant in the start of the show and  then  he keeps turning up for no clear reason  well no i take it back the reason is  clear he's going to be important later  on  but in the context of this season the  guy serves absolutely no purpose they  keep touching base and keeping tabs on  him but he's not doing anything that's  giving us any more information he's not  a particularly interesting character  unto himself  first we see his friend get infected we  go through the entire infection cycle  with that and then he gets back to his  apartment his brother's infected oh and  his mother's infected too oh it isn't  landlords in fact oh for crying out loud  we've seen it we  get it setting aside the mindless horde  of vampires our actual main villains are  a bit of a mixed bag too we've got  eichorst who is actually quite effective  he's basically a nazi vampire he factors  in very well into cetrakian's  past and his flashbacks and the actor  just portrays the part very well and  when we see his full vampire  look you know not trying to pass for  human it's interesting it's cool it's  creepy  but he's not the main bad guy the main  bad guy is the master  but the guy's basically just a stand in  for dracula first of all  and they were kind of getting away with  it until they actually revealed him  because  for at least the first half of the show  probably a little more than that he's  just he's this  huge cloaked figure we don't see a face  and it's kind of intriguing then  they finally show him to us and he looks  like this  let that sink in for just a second i  mean they basically took  the vampire design for someone like i  course and did  the saturday morning cartoon version of  it it i  almost did a spit take and burst out  laughing when i saw this thing  it's ridiculous look i'm not enjoying  crapping all over this show i wanted to  like it i  liked the pilot it had such potential  but it just it  it does almost nothing with it you know  there are a few bright spots i mentioned  kevin durant and david bradley as  vasilian as cetrakian they're  golden if the show had focused on them  primarily it would have been a million  times better already  sean aston works well as a very morally  compromised character because he's not  what you'd expect for that so he worked  there's some interesting stuff  particularly that's happening in the  finale  in terms of what we're learning about  these guys they call themselves the  agents we don't really know what's going  on with them they  seem to also be vampires but they're not  digging what the master is doing so it's  like  is he a rogue version from them so like  that's  interesting but i don't know if that's  gonna be enough to get me to come back  next season  but really very much like the walking  dead i feel like  i've seen all this before and it had the  potential to do something much more  interesting  now maybe if you're not as steeped in  vampire movies as  i am maybe it'll be new to you maybe  it'll be fresh to you and it'll be  interesting but for me  who's seen this stuff before it feels  like a retread it's a mashup of a couple  different things but it's all stuff i've  already seen  and it's presented well enough that it  wouldn't frustrate me so much if it  didn't keep dangling more interesting  ideas and then doing nothing with them  so while i am somewhat intrigued by the  stuff with the ancients and where it's  gonna go next season i don't think i  trust this show enough to do anything  interesting with that idea because i've  seen them blow  too many interesting possibilities  already like i said i kind of have to  compare it to walking dead most of the  people i know who really dig the walking  dead are people who have not seen a ton  of zombie  films i have so i feel like i've seen  pretty much everything the walking dead  has to offer me  and i feel the same about the strain so  if vampires are more of a peripheral  thing to you if you haven't seen a ton  of scary vampire movies well you know  what  this may work for you but if you're  anything like me at all there are better  ways to spend 13 hours of your life  so let's try and end this on an upbeat  what is your favorite  scary vampire film or tv show  whatever it is drop something down in  the comments let's talk about it until  next time this council  is adjourned

